  "worked_solution": "For a discrete random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}r(x)f(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)=(x-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[(X-1)^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-1)^{2}\\,f(x) \\\\  & =(1-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(2-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+(3-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 0.3+4\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0+0.3+2.4 \\\\  & =2.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
